Good, it's running. Here are the final working files.

## nodejs-configmap.yaml

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: nodejs-app-config
data:
  server.js: |
    const http = require("http");
    const port = 3000;

    const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {
      res.end("Hello from Node.js running inside Kubernetes!");
    });

    server.listen(port, () => {
      console.log(`Server running at port ${port}`);
    });
```

## nodejs-pod.yaml

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: nodejs-pod
  labels:
    app: nodejs
spec:
  containers:
  - name: nodejs
    image: node:18-alpine
    imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent
    command: ["node", "/usr/src/app/server.js"]
    ports:
    - containerPort: 3000
    volumeMounts:
    - name: app-code
      mountPath: /usr/src/app
  volumes:
  - name: app-code
    configMap:
      name: nodejs-app-config
```

If you ended up using `node:18` instead of `node:18-alpine`, change that one line to match what worked for you.

## Commands (from the manual)

```bash
kubectl apply -f nodejs-configmap.yaml
kubectl apply -f nodejs-pod.yaml
kubectl get pods
kubectl port-forward pod/nodejs-pod 3000:3000
```

Open `http://localhost:3000` for the output. Cleanup:

```bash
kubectl delete pods --all
kubectl delete svc --all
kubectl delete configmap nodejs-app-config
```

